Q: Can&#39;t stop page from reloading in SvelteKit after submitting form (with use:enhance and form actions) A: <p>If you want to stay on the page and keep your local state exactly as it is without SvelteKit trying to &quot;sync&quot; the DOM or re-run <code>load</code> functions, you should handle the <code>result</code> yourself instead of calling <code>update()</code>.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
    import { enhance } from '$app/forms';
    let thingsJsonString = '';

    // ... your logic
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;form
    method=&quot;POST&quot;
    action=&quot;?/updateThings&quot;
    use:enhance={() =&gt; {
        // This runs immediately upon submit
        return async ({ result }) =&gt; {
            // result.type can be 'success', 'error', 'redirect', or 'failure'
            if (result.type === 'success') {
                // The server returned { success: true }
                // We do nothing here, so the page stays exactly as is.
                console.log(&quot;Upload successful!&quot;);
            } else if (result.type === 'failure') {
                // Handle validation errors if you return fail(400, {...})
                console.error(&quot;Submission failed&quot;, result.data);
            }

            // Note: We are NOT calling update(). 
            // This prevents SvelteKit from re-running load functions 
            // and resetting the form state.
        };
    }}
&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;thingsJsonString&quot; bind:value={thingsJsonString}&gt;
    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: non-blocking I/O from keyboard to get key presses A: <p>You're on linux, so you can also use <code>ioctl(fileno(stdin), FIONREAD, &amp;bytes)</code> to get the number of bytes avalable, and only read the amount of reported bytes - this doesn't waste cpu cycles as a separate thread would, and is less cpu-intensive as <code>select</code> or <code>poll</code>.</p>
<p>Also, if you want to read keyboard input without waiting for the user to press <strong>ENTER</strong> you need to set the console to raw mode:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>termios old_termios;
tcgetattr(fileno(stdin),&amp;old_termios);
termios term_ios = old_termios;
term_ios.c_lflag &amp;= ~(ICANON | ECHO);
tcsetattr(fileno(stdin), TCSANOW, &amp;term_ios);
</code></pre>
<p>This stops the console from buffering input until the <code>Enter</code> key is pressed and also stops the automatic echo-ing of the input to the terminal (Which is usually something you want to do when you want non-blocking unbuffered input - if not, remove <code>| ECHO</code> from the code sample)</p>
<p>When terminating set it back to the original mode, so to not break normal terminal functionality:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>tcsetattr(fileno(stdin), TCSANOW, &amp;old_termios);
</code></pre>
